  {"date": "1997-06-22", "venue": "Loreley", "city": "St. Goarshausen", "state": "Rhineland-Palatinate", "gap": 1, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "First of many very strong '97 \"standard\" versions. Lots of \"NICU\"/\"Norwegian Wood\" theming. Quality sbd recording on the \"Spreadsheet.\"", "next": "Water in the Sky", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-06-25", "venue": "L\u2019Aeronef", "city": "Lille", "state": "Hauts-de-France", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "prev": "Dogs Stole Things", "next": "Billy Breathes", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-06-27", "venue": "Worthy Farm", "city": "Somerset", "state": "England", "gap": 1, "set": "1", "prev": "Poor Heart", "in": ">", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-06-29", "venue": "Roskilde Festival", "city": "Roskilde", "state": "Region Zealand", "gap": 1, "set": "1", "prev": "You Enjoy Myself", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-03", "venue": "Serenadenhof", "city": "N\u00fcremberg", "state": "Bavaria", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Trey shreds this one, and adds a lot of \"wah\" effects in the middle section. Great band-wide interplay at the peak.", "prev": "Beauty of My Dreams", "next": "Train Song", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-09", "venue": "Le Transbordeur", "city": "Lyon/Villeurbanne", "state": "Auvergne-Rh\u00f4ne", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Powerful Page solo. Like 7/3/97, very good Trey/Page interplay, similar to a good \"LxL\". And strong Trey. One of the first versions where the \"NICU\" riff appears immediately preceding the closing sequence.", "prev": "Dirt", "next": "Sweet Adeline", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-22", "venue": "Walnut Creek Amphitheater", "city": "Raleigh", "state": "NC", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Played during a thunder and lightning storm of Biblical proportion that prematurely ended Set I, you can hear the thunder crackling in the background. Clearly the storm electrified the band, and if you are a Page fan, this is a must-hear, incredibly intense version.", "prev": "Bye Bye Foot", "xnext": "Down with Disease", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-25", "venue": "Starplex Amphitheatre", "city": "Dallas", "state": "TX", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Joined by the late, great Bob Gullotti, this unique rendering (unsurprisingly) finds a percussive, pulsating groove, but just as the jam is about to peak with the traditional late-'90s \"Taste\" outro, it instead segues seamlessly into -> \"Ya Mar.\"", "note": "Bob Gullotti on a second drum set.", "out": "->", "prev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "in": "->", "next": "Ya Mar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-29", "venue": "Desert Sky Pavilion", "city": "Phoenix", "state": "AZ", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-> in from \"Twist.\" Pretty intense section towards the end of Trey's solo where the whole band is just hammering away. Great Mike on this one.", "prev": "Twist", "in": "->", "next": "Sample in a Jar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-03", "venue": "Gorge Amphitheatre", "city": "George", "state": "WA", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Around 6:30, this version comes very close to breaking free of \"Taste\" altogether into free form improvisation. Fantastic peak and finale.", "prev": "Lifeboy", "in": ">", "next": "Hello My Baby", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-09", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-> in from \"Ghost.\" Powerful version in which the whole band keeps rocking full tilt throughout the slot where Trey customarily takes the lead. Fish is the hidden gem holding rhythm in check while Trey and Page frenetically spiral up and up the scales.", "prev": "Ghost", "in": "->", "next": "Dogs Stole Things", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-14", "venue": "Darien Lake Performing Arts Center", "city": "Darien Center", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "prev": "Camel Walk", "xnext": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-17", "venue": "Loring Commerce Centre", "city": "Limestone", "state": "ME", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Powerhouse version from the Great Went. Riveting Page solo, skillful Trey solo, and spiraling crescendo finale.", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": "->", "next": "Carolina", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-11-16", "venue": "McNichols Arena", "city": "Denver", "state": "CO", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "prev": "Poor Heart", "next": "Hello My Baby", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-11-19", "venue": "Assembly Hall, University of Illinois", "city": "Champaign", "state": "IL", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "\"DEG\" tease from Trey. Another strong '97 version. Maybe not up there with the incredible batch from the Summer, but Trey's solo is patient, very gradually building up the intensity from a relaxed base. Page is rock solid.", "prev": "Makisupa Policeman", "in": ">", "xnext": "Possum", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-11-26", "venue": "Hartford Civic Center", "city": "Hartford", "state": "CT", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Unbelievable playing by Trey and the others as the band builds to a HUGE peak and then drives up over another. 7/22/97 is (literally) electrifying; 8/3/97 is unusually improvisational. This version is just phenomenal, with masterful contributions by all band members.", "prev": "Silent in the Morning", "xnext": "Character Zero", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-02", "venue": "CoreStates Spectrum", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "Dirt", "in": ">", "next": "The Star-Spangled Banner", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-12", "venue": "Pepsi Arena", "city": "Albany", "state": "NY", "gap": 7, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The Chairman of the Boards leads the way, but Big Red is no slouch either.", "out": ">", "prev": "Camel Walk", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-> in from an historic \"Sneakin' Sally.\" Strong version, but quite different from most of the Fall '97 versions. Here, Trey solos beautifully, but Page's role seems far more restrained. There is far less of a full band build towards the end than musical support for Trey's incredible soloing. To some ears, the best \"Taste\" ever. To others, it's too one dimensional.", "prev": "Sneakin' Sally Thru the Alley", "in": "->", "next": "Water in the Sky", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-04-04", "venue": "Providence Civic Center", "city": "Providence", "state": "RI", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Mike doesn't get a lot of mention on this chart, but he is really rock solid here, underpinning the harmonic base off of which Trey and Page shine. Still, this version doesn't have quite the \"extra mustard\" of many '97 versions.", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": ">", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-07-05", "venue": "Lucerna Theatre", "city": "Prague", "state": "Prague", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Birds of a Feather", "next": "Cavern", "nb": 1},
